title ' Gene-Expression & Radiomics — Comparative Pipelines
PCA-IPSO + SVM versus ABC-Selected 1-D CNN'

PROJECT OVERVIEW
This project reproduces and compares two recent cancer-classification workflows that address the “large-p, small-n” problem in different ways:

• Pipeline A – PCA-IPSO + SVM, from the paper “Osteosarcoma CT Radiomics: PCA-IPSO-SVM” (Wang et al., 2024, DOI 10.1016/j.media.2023.102748).
We apply it to tumour-typing on the microarray dataset GSE2109 (2 024 samples, 14 tissue classes).

• Pipeline B – ABC-Selected 1-D CNN, from the paper “Deep-Learning-Based Cancer Profiles Classification Using Gene Expression Data Profile” (Almarzouki et al., 2022, DOI 10.1093/bioinformatics/btac212).
We adapt it for binary lung tumour versus normal on dataset GSE19804 (60 tumour and 60 normal samples).

Everything needed to rerun the experiments—code, processed data, results and figures—is included in this repository.

REPOSITORY STRUCTURE

data/ processed expression matrices
 GSE2109_processed.csv
 GSE19804_processed.csv

notebooks/ executable Jupyter notebooks
 PAPER1_PCA_SVM.ipynb (Pipeline A, CPU-only)
 PAPER2_CNN.ipynb (Pipeline B, GPU recommended)

figures/ PNG images generated by the notebooks
 pca_scatter.png, svm_rf_roc.png, svm_confusion.png,
 cnn_loss_acc.png, tsne_cnn.png, cnn_confusion.png

results/ CSV outputs (metrics, confusion matrices)

env_paper1.yml Conda environment for Pipeline A
env_paper2.yml Conda environment for Pipeline B

README.txt this file

SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS

Pipeline A (PCA-IPSO + SVM):
• Python 3.11, scikit-learn ≥ 1.5, pandas, matplotlib

Pipeline B (ABC-Selected 1-D CNN):
• Python 3.11, TensorFlow ≥ 2.19, scikit-learn, seaborn
• CUDA 12.3 / cuDNN 8.9 for GPU acceleration (optional but recommended)

EXPECTED METRICS

Pipeline A (PCA-IPSO + SVM) should achieve:
Accuracy ≈ 0.924 Macro-F1 ≈ 0.921

Pipeline B (ABC 1-D CNN) should achieve:
Accuracy ≈ 0.867 Macro-F1 ≈ 0.867

If your results differ by more than two percentage points, please open an issue and attach the notebook log.

